factcheck by anthropic/claude-haiku-5-5: 4 problems
  The draft's headline and reel script say the rice was 'ration rice' (ரேஷன் அரிசி) and the caption says the Kulithalai/Karur details under that label, but the article only describes stock in the Tamil Nadu Civil Supplies Corporation warehouse (நுகர்பொருள் வாணிப கழகம்), not ration rice distributed to the public; this is an unsupported characterization.
  The reel script says the warehouse was inaugurated by the minister and that people complained 'to him' at the opening, but the article says the minister 'opened' the new warehouse and people complained to him there, so this is accurate; however the reel script states the complaint is the people's and that they are 'suffering greatly' (பெரும் அவதி), which matches the article.
  The reel script says the minister 'ordered' the station in-charge 'to be condemned' (கண்டிக்கப்பட்டார்), which matches; but the reel script and caption omit the fact that the minister questioned the official asking whether he would eat such rice, which is an important point of the article (the minister's direct remark) and is missing from the reel script.
  The reel script and caption say the minister gave the order to 'move old stock to the new building' and 'take measures to prevent worms', which matches the article, but the caption attributes the Kulithalai warehouse inspection to 'Kulithalai, Krishnarayapuram taluk warehouses' correctly; no mismatch, so no issue here.
